 CO3.4  WORKING-SET MODEL - measured on a locality-structured trace
==============================================================================
   Trace length        : 60,000 sampled references over 64 distinct pages
   True locality size  : 8 pages, drifting every 4,000 references

     Window Delta    mean WSS    peak WSS   min WSS   Interpretation
               10        5.89           8         1   too short - undercounts the locality
               25        7.72          15         1   too short - undercounts the locality
               50        8.02          15         1   tracks the true locality
              100        8.09          16         1   tracks the true locality
              250        8.24          16         1   tracks the true locality
              500        8.51          16         1   too long - absorbs stale localities
             1000        9.03          16         1   too long - absorbs stale localities

   Delta = 50-250 is the usable operating band: WSS settles on the
   generator's true locality of 8 pages. Too small a window starves the
   process; too large a window keeps dead pages resident and wastes
   frames that another guest needs. D = sum(WSS_i) computed with a
   window in this band is the demand figure the allocator must respect.

